{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"reasoning","text":"So there's no `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts`, no `tool-registration.test.ts`, etc. The task's target scope says to create `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` (a new test file) and modify `harness/specs/tasks/a1-layered-isolation-pilot.md` (add coverage guard + fix requiredTests), plus create gap spec/doc/acceptance/SHA256SUMS.\n\nLet me understand the acceptance criteria fully:\n\n1. 判据1 legacy fallback rate < 5%: deprecation-counters unit test asserts >5% → violated, <=5% → not violated (numeric threshold unchanged).\n2. 判据2 p99 ≤ 200ms: performance-budgets asserts p99 budget.\n3. 判据3 declaredPathViolationCount counted separately and tracked.\n4. 判据4 checkBudgetViolation('a1') returns action=degrade_to_legacy when rate>5%.\n5. Tool writeRiskProfile declaration and namespace rejection (claw.a4.tool.choice on a1) covered by tool-registration / trace-namespace-enforcement.\n6. Found and fixed spec drift: a1 spec's requiredTests originally missing counter test; added + coverage guard, original threshold bytes unchanged.\n7. Clean candidate targeted tests, typecheck, scoped lint, harness validate/dry-run, comms replay/compare pass, credential scan 0 hits, SHA256SUMS re-readable.\n\nSo the core deliverable is a new test file `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` that maps the 4 graduation criteria to executable evidence against the existing source. Plus fix the a1 spec's `requiredTests` (replace ghost test paths with real ones, add the counter test + a coverage guard), and add the gap spec, doc, acceptance.json, SHA256SUMS.\n\nWait — criterion 2 says \"performance-budgets asserts p99 budget\". Let me check if there's a \"performance-budgets\" module. Let me look at runtime-perf-report.test.ts and the trace-truncation test.\n\nLet me look at what the trace namespace enforcement looks like, and check the namespace-governance source."}}
